WEBVTT

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:03.000
Thank you.

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:18.350
Good morning, stranger.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:20.220
Hi, old timer.

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:22.640
Guess you don't remember me.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:24.140
Can't say to you.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:26.840
Guess there's something mighty familiar about you.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.940
Well, Jake, I guess it's a long time since you taught me how to...

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:31.650
Trap coyotes and ride rocks.

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:34.010
Jerry misses as I live.

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:37.100
Well, well, man, how you've grown.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.380
Well, I say, you're a regular mountain, ain't you?

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.670
Ha, sit down here and let's talk it over.

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:44.430
Well, there's not much to tell, Jake.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:48.000
Finished college, and true to your dad's last request,

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.320
you've come to live with me, eh?

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:50.640
That's right.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:53.210
Can't tell you how happy I am seeing you.

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:55.190
Well, I'm happy to be here, too, Jake.

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:58.060
How about the ranch? Cattle.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:01:59.860
There ain't no cattle.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:03.510
Rustler's got most of them, and I sold what was left.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:07.890
Can we stock it up again and start some other business?

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:10.070
Itching to get to work, eh?

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:15.600
Well, I was figuring on opening up the blacksmith shop, but...

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:21.580
What do you say we go in and fry us the chicken and gargle some coffee?

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:22.770
What do you say, huh?

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.110
Sounds like a good idea, especially the chicken.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.400
Well, no wonder this horse was limping.

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:06.450
Well, got him fixed up.

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:07.100
Yep.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:09.860
All sticked up a sharp rock.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.360
No, no, there ain't no charge.

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:14.030
Looks like you've been through plenty of water.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:17.630
Oh, yeah, tried a shortcut about 12 miles back in there and got stuck.

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:17.970
Oh.

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:19.870
That'd come right down through the middle of the creek.

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:22.060
That's where he went lame.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.320
Well, good luck to you.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:43.890
Hey, Jake, I just picked this up at the post office.

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:46.710
I bet I know who it's from.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:49.100
I was right.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:50.920
It's from Betty.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.590
That's right. It's from Betty.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:02.540
Betty?

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:04.110
My granddaughter.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:06.280
Did you know I had a granddaughter?

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:07.780
I certainly did not.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.800
Yes, siree. I'm her only living around it.

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:13.450
I've been sent her to college for a couple of years.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:15.880
She'll soon be here to live with me.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:17.460
Let's see what she's got to say.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:34.050
I just received my monthly check and thank you so much.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:38.660
I can't wait until school is over so I can come and live with you.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:43.360
Gee, you have three months more and I'll be keeping house for you.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:47.080
Please write me a nice long letter.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:50.430
I do so enjoy hearing from you.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:52.250
Lovingly Betty.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:56.380
She's a fine girl, Jerry.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:59.920
I'm going to do everything I can.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:00.740
to make her happy.

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:06.300
Freddie?

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:10.910
She's a damn dog.

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:11.890
Everybody feeds her.

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:29.680
Come on, so you want to play, eh?

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:34.260
Say, Jake, take a look.

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:36.960
That's that piece of quartz that came out of the horse's hook.

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:38.180
It's gold.

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:43.020
Say, there's a stringer in there bigger than a tenpenny nail.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:45.490
We only knew where it came from.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:46.480
I do know.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:50.620
That prospector said he was forced down the middle of a creek 12 miles out.

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:52.970
Well, there's only one creek out there, Jerry.

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:55.060
And it'll be a cinch to backtrack it.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:57.080
Well, we're on our way right now.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:59.970
And if we find anything, I know a dog that's gonna have a...

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.050
A porterhouse stake and a home for life.

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:03.070
You said it.

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:23.640
The stairs where he left the creek.

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:06.640
Wait a minute, look at that.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:10.560
Hey, that's the real stuff, son.

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:13.560
According to this sand, the creek's full of color.

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:31.590
Benson, what can I do for you?

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:33.630
First place, you fellers buy gold.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:37.300
Stuff, see what we got.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.810
Stuff, as good as I've ever seen.

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:54.020
Like somewhere.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:21.300
Let's see, $16 an ounce will come to $848.

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:25.770
Okay, we'll take that in currency if it's just the same to you.

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:27.710
Okay, all right, Joe.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:33.110
to bring in many times that amount.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:34.850
We think we've got a rich strike,

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:37.810
but we don't want anybody to know anything about it.

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:39.540
She'll tell us, won't you?

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:41.250
We're not telling anybody, Harris.

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:44.330
But when we do get ready to let the location be known,

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.190
you'll be the first ones in on it.

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:46.910
Thanks.

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:49.470
Come on, Jake, we gotta go buy a dog a porterhouse date.

00:08:52.570 --> 00:08:55.270
They made a rich strike, and it's up to us to locate it.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:59.180
I wouldn't mind having old man Benson's ranch either.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:02.300
He used to run cattle.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:08.200
Of course he doesn't know it, but I got most of them.

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:35.400
You know, Jake, it's a good thing we didn't file on that claim.

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:41.520
It had tipped the whole town off to the location and confined our operations.

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:44.060
As it is, we can work the whole creek.

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:50.360
Yeah. Your idea of crossing Windy Flats and entering the town from the other side sure had them puzzled.

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:57.400
Sure has. They've been back trailing us now for two months, and they always get stuck at Windy Flats.

00:09:58.040 --> 00:09:59.880
They think this mine's out in the middle of the desert.

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:02.060
Suppose we take a little rest, huh?

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:06.700
Just a few more days and Betty will be coming.

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:11.030
Well, don't you think we'd better be getting back

00:10:11.030 --> 00:10:12.750
and getting some of this dirt out of our hide?

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:14.540
Yeah, I reckon you're right.

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:18.040
You know, you want to sure look your best.

00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:53.640
We didn't get a bit of color

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:04.640
Now, wait a minute, I'll give you every nugget you find in the past.

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:07.980
Yeah, go on ahead and research it.

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:15.240
Here comes old Benson now, and Mason isn't with him.

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:17.160
Good. Are the papers all ready?

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:23.920
Everything, Jake.

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:27.010
All right, well, what luck this time?

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:27.870
Not so bad.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:29.800
Not so bad.

00:11:57.290 --> 00:11:58.850
That's a kind of picture to me.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:10.410
Let's see, $17 an ounce, that's $2,335.

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:13.120
How do you have it, in coin or bills?

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:14.860
Well, bills is easiest to carry.

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:18.630
All right, Joe. Sit down, Jake.

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:26.730
You've got to have your signature this time, Jake.

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:29.970
The government demands that they get a receipt for all monies paid out for...

00:12:34.348 --> 00:12:35.348
Good job.

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:38.420
a date on that, will ya?

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:29.350
Here's your money.

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:29.790
Thanks.

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:31.370
Give him a canteen, will you?

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:35.080
I'll be seeing you fellas again mighty soon.

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:35.980
Goodbye.

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:46.810
We got the deed to the ranch, and when he eventually disappears,

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:48.170
we'll have this recorded.

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:50.940
Let's see what we made on the nuggets.

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:57.410
How much did we get this time?

00:13:57.960 --> 00:13:59.720
$2,335.

00:14:02.268 --> 00:14:03.688
to hold out 500 of that.

00:14:04.476 --> 00:14:06.136
Pay on this blacksmith shop tomorrow.

00:14:07.676 --> 00:14:08.676
You know what Gary?

00:14:09.436 --> 00:14:13.036
I got an idea this is gonna be a valuable corner someday.

00:14:14.268 --> 00:14:15.868
We ain't golden and gold.

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:19.380
I think it's a good investment, Jake.

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:29.960
Whoa.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.860
Dad, you got a couple of bucks you can spare?

00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:35.450
Gambling again, eh?

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:37.940
Well, that's about all there is to do around this town.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:40.150
Gee, I wish I had a job.

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:41.870
So do I.

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:44.970
Remember, can't...

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:47.260
We're gonna keep this up forever. There's an end to everything.

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:47.720
Yeah.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:00.440
Come here a minute.

00:15:03.068 --> 00:15:06.068
Don't kick through that dough, you owe me. I'm telling the town everything.

00:15:06.204 --> 00:15:08.204
That'll just about throw your old man out of office.

00:15:09.052 --> 00:15:09.972
Where am I going to get it?

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:13.480
That's not up to me. I don't care where you get it or how you get it, but get it.

00:15:46.508 --> 00:15:47.348
Mr. William's in?

00:15:47.548 --> 00:15:49.228
Yes, Jake. You'll find him in his office.

00:15:49.348 --> 00:15:49.688
Thanks.

00:15:52.812 --> 00:15:52.992
Amen.

00:15:59.820 --> 00:15:59.980
Okay.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:00.760
I'm glad to see you.

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:03.640
Pay off my debt on the flex mix shop.

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:04.960
Fine.

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:06.370
Sit down.

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:20.360
I'll give you a receipt for your money.

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:23.440
We'll put it in the escrow.

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:26.380
Get your deed in a few days.

00:16:46.630 --> 00:16:48.300
How's the plane coming?

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:50.880
Still coughing up a few colors.

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:53.480
Won't be working it again until next spring.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:01.910
Howdy, sir.

00:17:02.390 --> 00:17:02.830
Hello.

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:38.130
Better send for the doctor, Sheriff.

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:44.980
Too late.

00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:46.980
You killed him, Jake.

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:50.160
I killed him.

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:52.240
Trying to deny it, are you?

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:53.690
Didn't I hear you fighting?

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:55.700
You were the only one in here, Mr. Benson.

00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:06.760
Somebody must have come in through the back door.

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:09.000
That's the only way it could have happened.

00:18:09.740 --> 00:18:10.900
Don't worry, old-timer.

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:12.980
I'll have you out of here in North Town.

00:18:45.070 --> 00:18:46.470
Mr. Benson's ranch, isn't it?

00:18:46.990 --> 00:18:48.480
Why, yes. Are you Betty?

00:18:50.340 --> 00:18:51.360
And you're Jerry Mason.

00:18:51.620 --> 00:18:53.420
Well, why didn't you let us know you were coming today?

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:55.580
I want a surprise, Sandy.

00:18:56.870 --> 00:18:59.230
So, where is it?

00:19:00.920 --> 00:19:10.270
Well, uh, you see, when he gets out in the hills prospecting, why, uh, well, it's pretty hard to tell when he is coming back. Won't you come in?

00:19:12.490 --> 00:19:17.970
Oh, gee, you don't know how glad I am to be here, but I just can't wait to see Grandy.

00:19:18.070 --> 00:19:20.390
Well, I'm gonna ride out and see if I can locate him.

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:21.670
Oh, I hope you find him.

00:19:28.990 --> 00:19:29.970
Now, just make yourself...

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:34.370
Well, thank you, and I have dinner ready for you and come back.

00:19:34.550 --> 00:19:35.550
Well, that'll be great.

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:36.340
Goodbye.

00:19:36.750 --> 00:19:36.950
Goodbye.

00:20:03.610 --> 00:20:04.430
Got any news, Jerry?

00:20:05.420 --> 00:20:08.810
Nope. I'm just going to give this bank the once-over.

00:20:09.340 --> 00:20:11.120
Well, this may not mean anything,

00:20:11.380 --> 00:20:15.110
but Al, the sheriff's son, has been flashing a roll of bills.

00:20:15.720 --> 00:20:17.680
Now, I know he hasn't done anything to earn it.

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:21.520
He just paid me for a horse I sold him.

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:29.580
Did Al Miller give you this money?

00:20:30.090 --> 00:20:30.870
He sure did.

00:20:31.110 --> 00:20:40.270
Where'd you get that money, Miller?

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:42.820
Why, I don't think that's none of your business.

00:20:43.210 --> 00:20:46.630
Well, I'm making it my business because that's part of the money Jake Benson paid the banker.

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:48.280
Now, just wait if you get it.

00:20:48.590 --> 00:20:51.060
As I told you before, it's none of your business.

00:22:31.560 --> 00:22:33.040
Tell these boys where you got that money.

00:22:33.500 --> 00:22:34.300
None of your business.

00:22:35.280 --> 00:22:38.670
I did it! I did it! Let me go.

00:22:39.780 --> 00:22:40.540
You hear that, boys?

00:23:10.910 --> 00:23:11.190
I'm factory one.

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:13.450
Get him, get him.

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:13.770
Get him, get him!

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:30.560
You got the best.

00:25:05.790 --> 00:25:07.640
I tell you, sheriff, Jake is innocent.

00:25:09.730 --> 00:25:10.470
Wait a minute, men.

00:25:11.930 --> 00:25:15.550
What you say is true, and my boy is guilty of this crime,

00:25:16.110 --> 00:25:18.470
I'll see that he gets the full penalty of the law.

00:25:19.420 --> 00:25:20.600
Here comes, Mason, now.

00:25:20.700 --> 00:25:21.000
Down.

00:25:21.140 --> 00:25:21.660
There he comes.

00:25:36.200 --> 00:25:39.850
Halton Miller, I arrest you for attempted murder and robbery.

00:25:40.800 --> 00:25:44.860
And I'm going to do my duty in helping to exact the full penalty for your crime.

00:25:47.650 --> 00:25:49.550
Sorry, Sheriff, but it had to be your son.

00:26:14.550 --> 00:26:20.080
I'm sorry, Benson.

00:26:21.380 --> 00:26:22.120
That's all right.

00:26:26.120 --> 00:26:27.120
Just how you feel.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:31.240
The rest of the bank's money, Sheriff.

00:26:47.530 --> 00:26:48.290
One of them things.

00:26:51.700 --> 00:26:54.810
Mighty good thing you're out.

00:26:55.170 --> 00:26:56.790
Because Betty's home waiting for you.

00:26:56.890 --> 00:26:59.620
Betty was jumping the husband.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:01.080
Well, maybe you think I wasn't one.

00:27:07.920 --> 00:27:09.220
Well, well, well.

00:27:09.850 --> 00:27:13.620
I'm never going to see you.

00:27:13.900 --> 00:27:17.580
Not so myself for a while, but thanks to Jerry, here I am.

00:27:18.270 --> 00:27:19.690
Dinner all ready for you.

00:27:19.890 --> 00:27:21.730
Yeah, and I'm sure ready for dinner.

00:27:24.800 --> 00:27:27.710
And Cracky, that's the best dinner I've had in years.

00:27:27.850 --> 00:27:29.050
And that goes for me, too.

00:27:30.160 --> 00:27:32.060
It isn't going to be very hard to please you two.

00:27:32.420 --> 00:27:35.220
Well, son, we won't be working the mine again the next spring.

00:27:35.760 --> 00:27:38.040
You know, we can't afford to miss meals like this.

00:27:38.860 --> 00:27:40.960
I think I'll go out tomorrow and hide the sluice box.

00:27:42.230 --> 00:27:44.530
In fact, I'll stake out three claims along the creek,

00:27:44.630 --> 00:27:45.430
and you can file on them.

00:27:46.360 --> 00:27:49.430
After all, you know, better be on the safe side.

00:27:50.260 --> 00:27:52.440
While you're gone, I'll take Betty around the ranch

00:27:52.440 --> 00:27:54.220
and shore the town and our blacksmith.

00:27:54.380 --> 00:27:54.560
Sure.

00:27:54.980 --> 00:27:56.940
And you can figure on me being here for dinner.

00:27:57.370 --> 00:27:58.250
All right, Grandy.

00:28:01.340 --> 00:28:04.740
This town is located about six miles off that spur.

00:28:09.440 --> 00:28:11.500
Hey, Mason, can I see you a minute?

00:28:12.570 --> 00:28:13.570
Pardon me a moment, Betty.

00:28:22.330 --> 00:28:24.910
You know they're taking young Miller over to Cedar City?

00:28:25.070 --> 00:28:25.910
Is that south?

00:28:26.190 --> 00:28:27.950
Yeah, and I thought you might like to know that

00:28:28.070 --> 00:28:29.970
Banker William is gonna pull...

00:28:30.520 --> 00:28:32.220
Well, that is good news.

00:28:41.210 --> 00:28:42.250
Jake Benson around?

00:28:43.080 --> 00:28:45.400
Why, no. He went to his claim this morning.

00:28:45.970 --> 00:28:47.290
But he'll be back this afternoon.

00:28:48.590 --> 00:28:50.300
Oh, thanks.

00:28:57.640 --> 00:28:59.980
Benson's out to his claim and he won't be back till late this afternoon.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:02.160
This is just what we've been waiting for.

00:29:19.100 --> 00:29:22.090
...nuggets that Jerry don't know nothing about.

00:29:23.710 --> 00:29:26.070
Won't he and Betty be surprised when they hear that?

00:29:32.590 --> 00:29:33.210
Come on, Brady.

00:30:07.900 --> 00:30:09.440
Guess we got here just in time.

00:30:25.760 --> 00:30:26.640
Drop your hands, Benson.

00:30:27.650 --> 00:30:29.930
We've decided it's about time you were tipping us off.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:31.240
of this goldfield of yours.

00:30:31.640 --> 00:30:33.380
Oh, so that's your game, eh?

00:30:34.100 --> 00:30:36.000
Well, Jerry and me found that goldfield,

00:30:36.750 --> 00:30:38.430
and we ain't tipping it off to nobody.

00:30:39.220 --> 00:30:53.580
I've done for.

00:30:53.910 --> 00:30:56.520
Yeah, there's a canteen on that patch.

00:30:57.040 --> 00:30:58.480
Come on, we've got to catch that mule.

00:31:23.160 --> 00:31:23.980
Sure enough.

00:31:31.020 --> 00:31:31.460
Thank you.

00:32:01.910 --> 00:32:15.040
Thank you.

00:32:32.200 --> 00:32:34.170
No use here. I can't get it.

00:32:34.310 --> 00:32:36.310
Well, come on. We've got to get out of here and get back to town.

00:32:36.470 --> 00:32:38.620
We can't afford to be seen here. Get your heart.

00:32:41.350 --> 00:32:44.530
Now, listen, Freddy. I want you to go get Jerry.

00:32:45.360 --> 00:32:48.180
You understand? Go get Jerry.

00:32:48.920 --> 00:32:49.380
Go get him.

00:33:19.320 --> 00:33:26.600
Oh, yeah.

00:33:30.760 --> 00:33:31.380
Sure is.

00:33:31.900 --> 00:33:33.300
Say, here comes his pack.

00:33:36.800 --> 00:33:42.940
What do you suppose has happened?

00:33:44.130 --> 00:33:45.850
I don't know, but I'm gonna find out.

00:33:51.720 --> 00:33:53.200
What's all the excitement about?

00:33:53.420 --> 00:33:56.220
Why, old Jake Ford and his pack gave him a lottery.

00:33:56.750 --> 00:33:57.190
That's all?

00:33:57.450 --> 00:33:57.610
Yeah.

00:34:00.060 --> 00:34:01.880
There's a potty in the potty.

00:34:03.740 --> 00:34:05.300
He never did this before.

00:34:09.000 --> 00:34:13.240
Friday! Where's Jake?

00:34:19.870 --> 00:34:22.030
You better go back home and wait till you hear from me, Betty.

00:34:22.380 --> 00:34:22.960
All right, Jerry.

00:35:23.420 --> 00:35:25.640
What's the matter, old-timer? Are you all right?

00:35:26.010 --> 00:35:28.820
I'm only a little dizzy. I'm getting better every minute.

00:35:29.250 --> 00:35:29.970
They only nick me.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:33.060
What are you talking about? Who nicked you?

00:35:33.180 --> 00:35:36.040
I'll tell you all about it on the way home. Come on.

00:35:48.060 --> 00:35:49.900
Remember now, son, not a word to Betty.

00:36:03.550 --> 00:36:05.210
Oh, you're hurt.

00:36:05.470 --> 00:36:07.010
Oh, king, nothing tall.

00:36:07.580 --> 00:36:09.580
Horse rode me a little square on my head.

00:36:09.950 --> 00:36:11.230
What I need is good feed.

00:36:11.650 --> 00:36:14.430
Oh, well, I'll run right uptown and get you something nice then.

00:36:14.860 --> 00:36:16.940
Well, don't tell anyone that your granddad is here.

00:36:18.800 --> 00:36:28.160
Son, open up that trunk and get out my make-up case, will you?

00:36:28.580 --> 00:36:29.480
Make-up case?

00:36:29.760 --> 00:36:29.900
Yeah.

00:36:36.840 --> 00:36:37.960
This here'll stop it bleeding.

00:36:39.690 --> 00:36:40.750
What in the world's this?

00:36:41.550 --> 00:36:45.470
Oh, that's just a souvenir of my old theatrical days.

00:36:46.530 --> 00:36:48.230
I didn't know you were an actor, Jake.

00:36:48.540 --> 00:36:52.920
Yep, wore that when I played in a show called Charlie's Ant.

00:36:53.290 --> 00:36:53.510
Yeah?

00:36:55.720 --> 00:36:56.840
What the heck is this?

00:36:57.640 --> 00:36:59.970
Son, that's the thing that...

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:02.600
that helped make Anna Held and Lillian Russell famous.

00:37:03.040 --> 00:37:05.020
Oh, I see. Up here like this, eh?

00:37:05.360 --> 00:37:09.820
Oh! Ha ha! You darn yearling, you got it in the wrong spot!

00:37:22.620 --> 00:37:25.460
Mason, has Benson come in yet?

00:37:26.040 --> 00:37:29.890
Not yet. If he doesn't get in by night, I'm going looking.

00:37:31.970 --> 00:37:35.890
We just called to find out when we could take possession of this ranch.

00:37:36.820 --> 00:37:39.490
Take possession? I don't understand.

00:37:40.880 --> 00:37:42.720
Well, maybe Benson didn't tell you,

00:37:42.800 --> 00:37:44.920
but we bought this ranch a few days ago.

00:37:46.280 --> 00:37:48.880
That's strange. Funny he didn't tell me.

00:37:49.890 --> 00:37:50.730
You got a bill of sale?

00:37:51.360 --> 00:37:53.340
Why, certainly. It's the office.

00:37:54.520 --> 00:37:56.220
Well, then I'll have Jake drop in tomorrow,

00:37:56.280 --> 00:37:58.670
and he can advise you when he's getting out.

00:37:59.410 --> 00:37:59.970
That'll be fun.

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:02.860
We're anxious to get started on the improvements on the place.

00:38:03.550 --> 00:38:18.720
What are they talking about? I ain't sold no ranch.

00:38:18.860 --> 00:38:20.540
Have you signed any papers lately, Jake?

00:38:20.740 --> 00:38:23.800
No, I think so. Wait a minute.

00:38:23.980 --> 00:38:24.560
Yes, I did.

00:38:24.960 --> 00:38:27.620
I signed a receipt for the money we got for them last nuggets.

00:38:27.820 --> 00:38:28.980
Well, did you look at it closely?

00:38:29.220 --> 00:38:29.440
No.

00:38:30.410 --> 00:38:33.050
Well, that's it, then. You probably signed a bill of sale for the ranch.

00:38:33.560 --> 00:38:35.080
That's why they were trying to get rid of you.

00:38:35.740 --> 00:38:38.280
They figured they could claim the ranch then and nobody could deny it.

00:38:38.610 --> 00:38:41.110
That dirty, low-down polecats.

00:38:41.480 --> 00:38:44.420
But we'll get them. You wait till my headache's better tomorrow.

00:38:44.790 --> 00:38:46.330
We'll give them the surprise of their life.

00:38:47.040 --> 00:38:48.920
Hey, but you better go file on them claims.

00:38:49.970 --> 00:38:52.430
Take that canteen of nuggets and leave it at the bank this time.

00:39:03.450 --> 00:39:05.070
Here's the location of them three claims.

00:39:05.540 --> 00:39:08.000
Now, there's one for Betty, one for you, and one for me.

00:39:08.750 --> 00:39:11.310
Right. You better lie down and get some sleep, Jake.

00:39:11.640 --> 00:39:14.650
Don't you forget yourself. Remember, I'm supposed to be dead.

00:39:14.910 --> 00:39:15.870
Oh, I ain't forgetting.

00:39:48.910 --> 00:39:49.610
There's Mason.

00:39:59.020 --> 00:39:59.900
Isn't that old Jake's can?

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:02.730
on the saddle? Let's go see.

00:40:02.970 --> 00:40:22.470
We must have taken it off the borough before we got there.

00:40:41.680 --> 00:40:42.460
How did we get there, boys?

00:40:42.760 --> 00:40:43.560
Oh, hello, hello.

00:40:43.900 --> 00:40:47.300
Uh, you see, Sheriff, we recognize this canteen.

00:40:48.020 --> 00:40:49.940
It belongs to old Jake Benson.

00:40:50.980 --> 00:40:52.940
Whenever Jake brought in his nuggets to us,

00:40:52.940 --> 00:40:55.480
unknown to anyone else, he brought them in this canteen.

00:40:56.620 --> 00:40:59.880
We thought it was kind of funny that old Jake's disappeared.

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:02.150
and Mason should have this.

00:41:02.920 --> 00:41:03.580
Where is Mason?

00:41:04.100 --> 00:41:05.160
He went in the courthouse.

00:41:06.290 --> 00:41:07.890
Please go in there and see what Mason's doing.

00:41:09.360 --> 00:41:10.880
I reckon he can explain this.

00:41:12.900 --> 00:41:13.700
Better be able to.

00:41:30.320 --> 00:41:32.220
He's filing on a mining claim, Sheriff.

00:41:33.120 --> 00:41:35.700
Ah, probably old Jake's claim.

00:41:36.910 --> 00:41:38.910
Well, we'll just wait till he gets here.

00:41:46.990 --> 00:41:49.780
Howdy, boys. What's all the pow-wow about?

00:41:50.710 --> 00:41:53.310
Just how did you come to have this canteen of nuggets?

00:41:54.400 --> 00:41:56.320
I don't care to answer that question, Harris.

00:41:58.060 --> 00:41:59.740
Claim are you just filing on, Mason?

00:42:00.730 --> 00:42:01.590
My own claim.

00:42:02.810 --> 00:42:04.950
Do you know anything about Jake Benson's disappearance?

00:42:05.310 --> 00:42:06.930
Yes, I know he hasn't come back.

00:42:08.230 --> 00:42:11.290
Sorry, Mason, but I'll have to hold you until we can locate Jake.

00:42:13.370 --> 00:42:13.950
Fair enough.

00:42:14.620 --> 00:42:16.120
When do I get my preliminary hearing?

00:42:17.260 --> 00:42:18.300
First thing tomorrow morning.

00:42:20.290 --> 00:42:22.010
You better take charge of those nuggets, Sheriff.

00:42:38.070 --> 00:42:44.880
What are they going to do to Mason?

00:42:45.200 --> 00:42:46.280
They think he killed old Jason.

00:42:46.480 --> 00:42:46.780
They do.

00:42:49.260 --> 00:42:50.260
Then what's wrong?

00:42:50.620 --> 00:42:51.520
Mason's up for murder.

00:42:52.260 --> 00:42:52.600
Murder?

00:42:52.940 --> 00:42:53.260
Yes.

00:43:03.550 --> 00:43:05.850
May I please have a moment, Mr. Mason?

00:43:06.680 --> 00:43:08.870
Yes, I guess so. Go ahead.

00:43:12.800 --> 00:43:15.950
Now listen, they think I've murdered your granddad.

00:43:16.200 --> 00:43:18.820
Don't say anything to anyone, but hurry home and tell Jake

00:43:18.820 --> 00:43:20.960
that I have a preliminary hearing in the morning

00:43:20.960 --> 00:43:23.760
and for him to get there without being seen by anyone.

00:43:24.000 --> 00:43:25.860
All right, Jake. Bye.

00:43:29.220 --> 00:43:29.380
Bye.

00:43:55.240 --> 00:43:56.780
They got Jerry locked up in jail.

00:43:57.230 --> 00:43:57.810
What's that?

00:43:58.330 --> 00:43:59.370
They think he murdered you.

00:44:00.092 --> 00:44:00.712
very good.

00:44:33.804 --> 00:44:35.124
I don't make gentlemen, but...

00:44:35.404 --> 00:44:36.624
I'm looking for the courthouse.

00:44:36.972 --> 00:44:38.252
You're standing right in it, madam.

00:44:40.076 --> 00:44:40.916
Oh, good.

00:44:41.292 --> 00:44:41.792
Thank you.

00:44:42.444 --> 00:44:44.544
I do love murder trials, don't you?

00:44:45.676 --> 00:44:48.596
But if I were a murderer, I'd much prefer the electric chair.

00:44:48.876 --> 00:44:50.556
than to have a rope around my neck.

00:44:50.764 --> 00:44:51.324
Wouldn't you?

00:44:51.884 --> 00:44:52.524
Listen, lady.

00:44:52.908 --> 00:44:53.748
We're not interested.

00:44:55.212 --> 00:44:57.212
But you're going to be...

00:45:01.340 --> 00:45:02.980
Here comes the sheriff and makes them off.

00:45:05.756 --> 00:45:07.596
My goodness, my big feet.

00:45:12.316 --> 00:45:13.576
Just a minute, boys. Check your hardware.

00:45:28.348 --> 00:45:29.188
Come on, let's get in here.

00:45:30.120 --> 00:45:30.620
It's hard.

00:46:34.444 --> 00:46:35.384
hear you, hear you, hear you.

00:46:36.492 --> 00:46:38.932
in Omaha County is now open. Judge McGill presiding.

00:46:39.404 --> 00:46:41.484
Everybody be seated and come to a media order.

00:46:48.812 --> 00:46:49.652
the runner.

00:46:50.412 --> 00:46:53.912
Before you proceed further with this case, there's a few words I'd like to say.

00:46:54.412 --> 00:46:55.512
What is your name, madam?

00:46:56.012 --> 00:46:57.772
Veronica Mehippo Benson.

00:46:58.860 --> 00:46:59.960
Any relation to Jake?

00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:21.310
this year it's the same and I'm going

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:30.720
to the point, madam.

00:47:31.276 --> 00:47:31.776
Well...

00:47:32.524 --> 00:47:34.164
I know who shot Jake Benson.

00:47:36.044 --> 00:47:37.624
The men are in this court, Your Honor.

00:47:38.220 --> 00:47:41.460
And I advise the sheriff not to let anyone leave this room.

00:47:44.972 --> 00:47:46.052
Tried to steal his mind.

00:47:46.956 --> 00:47:48.296
They tried to steal his ranch.

00:47:49.292 --> 00:47:50.472
And they shut him down in.

00:47:50.732 --> 00:47:51.732
cold blood.

00:47:52.812 --> 00:47:53.732
How do you know this?

00:47:54.860 --> 00:47:56.980
Because I was there when it happened, Your Honor.

00:48:07.740 --> 00:48:09.620
Sheriff, go ahead, Miss Benson, then.

00:49:07.860 --> 00:49:08.760
I'll do the driver.

00:53:40.460 --> 00:53:42.040
All right, now, folks, that looks fine.

00:53:42.540 --> 00:53:44.080
Now, just a minute. Relax for a minute.

00:53:44.620 --> 00:53:45.300
Now, here we go.

00:53:46.410 --> 00:53:49.030
You must remember that I spent most all of the afternoon

00:53:49.030 --> 00:53:50.360
trying to get you in position.

00:53:51.040 --> 00:53:52.820
Now, hold it. Just like that.

00:53:54.010 --> 00:53:56.040
Still. Hold it. Hold it.

00:53:59.740 --> 00:53:59.980
Ready now?

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:00.160
I don't know.
